  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone and CD276 antigen, mediated through a series of targets that are all part of the thioredoxin family. This pathway involves 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone acting as a target for multiple compounds, including Phorone, Flavipin, and Isotorachrysone-6-O-alpha-D-ribofuranoside, which in turn target CD276 antigen. The high scores across the three paths indicate a strong, albeit indirect, connection between the drug and the antigen, likely through a shared biological mechanism involving redox regulation or protein interaction. The presence of multiple targets in the thioredoxin pathway suggests that 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone may influence cellular processes through this network, potentially modulating CD276 antigen function. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of thioredoxin in mediating the drug’s effects, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
